'</div>'))
,p_list_template_current=>'<li class="amc-TSpeedDial-item is-current"><a class="amc-TSpeedDial-link" href="#LINK#" aria-current="page"><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-label"><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-text">#TEXT#</span><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-hint">#A01#</span></span><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-mini"><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-icon fa #ICON_CSS_CLASSES#" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></a></li>'
,p_list_template_noncurrent=>'<li class="amc-TSpeedDial-item"><a class="amc-TSpeedDial-link" href="#LINK#"><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-label"><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-text">#TEXT#</span><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-hint">#A01#</span></span><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-mini"><span class="amc-TSpeedDial-icon fa #ICON_CSS_CLASSES#" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></a></li>'
,p_list_template_name=>'AMC Speed Dial'
,p_internal_name=>'AMC_TPL_SPEED_DIAL'
,p_javascript_file_urls=>'#APP_FILES#amc-templates/amc-tpl-speed-dial.js'
,p_theme_id=>42
,p_css_file_urls=>'#APP_FILES#amc-templates/amc-tpl-speed-dial.css'
,p_a01_label=>'Hint'
,p_list_template_comment=>'List template for a List region. The entries open from a floating action button: pointer hover opens the dial, a click or tap on the button keeps it open, and keyboard users press Enter or Space on the button and then Tab through the actions. The first entry sits closest to the button. User Defined Attribute 1 is an optional hint under the label, for example ''Ctrl+Alt+N'' or ''3 drafts''. The button text ''Quick actions'' lives in Before List Entry; edit it there to translate it. The optional JavaScript file closes the dial with Escape, on a click outside and when focus leaves it. Template options set the corner (Start corner, Top corner), the direction (Quarter arc), Icon only button and Float on page. By default the region reserves room for the fan; Float on page pins the button to the browser window corner instead. Under reduced motion the dial opens without movement; browsers without CSS trigonometry show the arc as a stack; on touch screens the arc falls back to the stack so labels stay visible.'
);
end;
/
